  "specDocument": "## Rules\n\n| ID | Description |\n|----|-------------|\n| R1 | **Construction copies input**: `ImmutableIntList.of(Collection<Integer>)` creates an instance that contains a copy of the supplied collection's elements in iteration order. The supplied collection must not contain `null` elements. Subsequent modifications to the original collection must not affect the instance.\n| R2 | **Immutability of exposed collection**: `asList()` returns an *unmodifiable* `List<Integer>` view of the instance's elements. Any mutating operation on the returned list (e.g., `add`, `remove`, `clear`) must throw `UnsupportedOperationException`. The view always reflects the current state of the instance but cannot be used to change it.\n| R3 | **Equality by content**: Two `ImmutableIntList` instances are equal (`equals`) iff they contain the same elements in the same order. `hashCode` must be consistent with this definition. Instances never contain `null` elements.\n| R4 | **Add returns new instance**: `add(int value)` returns a new `ImmutableIntList` containing all elements of the original instance followed by `value`. The original instance remains unchanged.\n| R5 | **Remove returns new instance**: `remove(int value)` returns a new `ImmutableIntList` that contains all elements of the original instance except the *first* occurrence of `value`. If the value is not present, the returned instance is equal to the original. The original instance remains unchanged.\n\n## Worked Examples\n\n| Rules | Input | Expected |\n|-------|-------|----------|\n| R1,R2,R3,R4,R5 | ```java\nList<Integer> src = new ArrayList<>(List.of(1, 2, 3));\nImmutableIntList a = ImmutableIntList.of(src);\nsrc.add(4); // mutate source after construction\nImmutableIntList b = a.add(5);\nList<Integer> view = b.asList();\ntry {\n    view.remove(0); // should throw UnsupportedOperationException\n} catch (UnsupportedOperationException ignored) {}\n``` | `a` holds `[1,2,3]` (unchanged by `src` mutation). `b` holds `[1,2,3,5]`. The `view` reflects `[1,2,3,5]` and attempts to modify it throw, leaving `b` unchanged. `a.equals(ImmutableIntList.of(List.of(1,2,3)))` is `true`.\n| R1,R2,R4,R5,R3 | ```java\nImmutableIntList empty = ImmutableIntList.of(List.of());\nImmutableIntList added = empty.add(10);\nImmutableIntList removed = added.remove(10);\n``` | `empty` holds `[]`. `added` holds `[10]`. `removed` holds `[]` and is equal to `empty`.\n\n## Design\n\n| Type | Role | Template status |\n|------|------|-----------------|\n| ImmutableIntList | Value type that stores an ordered collection of `int` values immutably. Students must implement its behavior. | stubbed |\n\n## Public API\n\n### ImmutableIntList\n```java\npublic final class ImmutableIntList {\n    public static ImmutableIntList of(Collection<Integer> elements) { ... }\n    public ImmutableIntList add(int value) { ... }\n    public ImmutableIntList remove(int value) { ... }\n    public List<Integer> asList() { ... }\n    @Override\n    public boolean equals(Object o) { ... }\n    @Override\n    public int hashCode() { ... }\n}\n```\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n| ID | Owner type | Observable responsibility | Weight | After due date |\n|----|------------|---------------------------|--------|----------------|\n| S1 | ImmutableIntList | Verify that construction copies the input collection and that later mutations of the source do not affect the instance (R1). | 3 | no |\n| S2 | ImmutableIntList | Verify that `asList()` returns an unmodifiable view: reading works, mutating throws `UnsupportedOperationException` (R2). | 2 | no |\n| S3 | ImmutableIntList | Verify `equals` and `hashCode` obey content equality (R3). | 3 | no |\n| S4 | ImmutableIntList | Verify `add` returns a new instance with the element appended while leaving the original unchanged (R4). | 3 | no |\n| S5 | ImmutableIntList | Verify `remove` returns a new instance without the first occurrence of the given value, original unchanged, and that removing a non‑present value yields an equal instance (R5). | 3 | no |\n\n## Contract Risk Inventory\n\n| Seam | Rules | Admitted partitions | Excluded inputs |\n|------|-------|---------------------|-----------------|\n| S1 | R1 | S1.P1: empty collection; S1.P2: non‑empty collection; S1.P3: collection with duplicate values | null elements in the supplied collection |\n| S2 | R2 | S2.P1: view is queried (read operations succeed); S2.P2: mutating view throws `UnsupportedOperationException` | null elements in the underlying instance (cannot occur) |\n| S3 | R3 | S3.P1: equal content same order; S3.P2: same elements different order; S3.P3: different sizes; S3.P4: compare with `null` or different type | null elements in either instance |\n| S4 | R4 | S4.P1: add to empty list; S4.P2: add to non‑empty list; S4.P3: add extreme int values (`Integer.MIN_VALUE`, `Integer.MAX_VALUE`) | none |\n| S5 | R5 | S5.P1: remove existing value (first occurrence); S5.P2: remove value not present; S5.P3: remove from empty list; S5.P4: remove when multiple identical values present (only first removed) | none |\n\n## Decision Ledger\n\n| Decision | Provenance | Why necessary | Observable |\n|----------|------------|---------------|------------|\n| Use `List<Integer>` as internal representation | EXPLICIT_BRIEF (collection value type) | Provides ordered collection semantics required by equality rule | R3 behavior depends on order |\n| Copy input collection on construction | NECESSARY_OPERATIONAL_CHOICE | Guarantees immutability against external mutations (R1) | R1 outcome |\n| Return an *unmodifiable* view from `asList()` | NECESSARY_OPERATIONAL_CHOICE | Gives deterministic, testable contract for R2 without allowing mutable copies | R2 outcome |\n| `remove` deletes first occurrence only | EXPLICIT_BRIEF (derived operations must be deterministic) | Provides deterministic behavior for tests | R5 partitions S5.P4 |\n| Disallow `null` elements in the collection | INPUT_DOMAIN_ASSUMPTION | Simplifies equality and collection handling; avoids undefined behavior | All rules operate on non‑null ints |\n\n## Diagram\n\nNo – the exercise involves a single collaborating type; no additional diagram needed.\n",
